{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.98,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C12"],
      "pins": ["C12.1", "C12.2"],
      "nets": ["BAT+", "GND"],
      "observed": "C12 is specified in the netlist as value \"2.2mF\" (2.2 millifarads) and the SPICE deck confirms a value of 2.2m (2.2 mF). Its footprint is an 0805 capacitor footprint.",
      "expected": "The specification states C12 should be 2.2 µF (microfarads), the input capacitor on BAT+ to GND. A 2.2 mF capacitor is 1000× too large and cannot physically fit an 0805 footprint.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C12 (2.2 µF) on BAT+→GND is the input cap"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C12\") (value \"2.2mF\") (footprint \"Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.18x1.45mm_HandSolder\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C12 BAT+ 0 2.2m"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The input capacitor is 1000× oversized, causing extreme inrush current, possible failure of the USB/DC source or regulator, and an assembly impossibility because a 2.2 mF capacitor cannot be placed in an 0805 footprint.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "Display_Power_Switch"],
      "observed": "C1 is specified in the netlist as value \"0.1uF/16V\". The SPICE deck lists C1 as 0.1uF.",
      "expected": "The specification states that C1, C5, C7, C8, C9 and C10 should all be 1 µF/25 V to match the PDI default for the EPD driver circuit. C1 is therefore 10× too low in capacitance and has an insufficient 16 V voltage rating versus the required 25 V.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\") (value \"0.1uF/16V\") (footprint \"Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.18x1.45mm_HandSolder\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C1 0 Display_Power_Switch 0.1uF"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The EPD boost/charge-pump circuit has reduced capacitance and a lower voltage rating than intended, which can degrade display power sequencing, cause unstable EPD operation, and risk capacitor failure if boost voltages exceed 16 V.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["C11"],
      "pins": ["C11.1", "C11.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C11-Pad1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "C11 is a 0.1uF capacitor with pin 2 on GND and pin 1 on a net named \"unconnected-(C11-Pad1)\". Its footprint is \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\", an inductor footprint, not a capacitor footprint.",
      "expected": "A capacitor should have both terminals connected to circuit nodes (e.g., a supply rail and GND) and should use a capacitor footprint. The specification does not mention C11, so an unconnected capacitor with an inductor footprint is not consistent with standard design practice.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C11\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"59\") (name \"unconnected-(C11-Pad1)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"C11\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C11 unconnected-_C11-Pad1_ 0 0.1u"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "C11 has no electrical function as connected. If it was intended as a decoupling capacitor for a supply rail, that rail lacks the intended bypass, potentially increasing noise or instability. The inductor footprint also makes assembly incorrect for a capacitor.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain clear deviations: C12 is 2.2 mF instead of the specified 2.2 µF, C1 is 0.1 µF/16 V instead of the specified 1 µF/25 V, and C11 is an unconnected capacitor with an inductor footprint. These errors would prevent the board from behaving as intended."
}

